# .cursorrules — Car Inpainting Demo (CS331 · Streamlit)

## Project
Streamlit demo for occluded car inpainting.
SD v1.5 base + LoRA (PEFT) + ControlNet + IP-Adapter.
Drawing canvas via streamlit-drawable-canvas.

## Critical model IDs (never change)
- SD base:     runwayml/stable-diffusion-inpainting   ← LoRA trained on v1.5
- ControlNet:  lllyasviel/control_v11p_sd15_canny
- IP-Adapter:  h94/IP-Adapter / models / ip-adapter-plus_sd15.bin
- LoRA path:   outputs/lora_weights/r8/best/

## 4 pipeline objects (loaded once via @st.cache_resource)
  pipe_base      → Config A
  lora_pipe_base → Config E  (LoRA fused, merge_and_unload)
  pipe_cn        → Configs B, C  (IP-Adapter loaded, scale=0 when not used)
  lora_pipe_cn   → Configs F, G  (LoRA fused + IP-Adapter loaded)

## Canny params (exact from notebooks)
  low=80, high=150, mask_dilate=5px, zero edges inside mask

## Visible patch (IP-Adapter input)
  Replace masked pixels with mean color of visible region

## Streamlit-specific rules
  @st.cache_resource on load_pipelines() — never reload on rerun
  @st.cache_data NOT for pipelines (tensors not serializable)
  load_pipelines() called at module level, not inside button callback
  canvas image_data is RGBA numpy — extract mask from alpha channel (> 10)
  Disable IP-Adapter on non-IP configs via pipe.set_ip_adapter_scale(0.0)

## Never do
  stabilityai/stable-diffusion-2-inpainting  ← wrong base model
  Reload LoRA inside inpaint() per call
  controlnet_aux.CannyDetector  ← use cv2.Canny directly
  xformers  ← use enable_attention_slicing("auto")
  st.cache_data on torch models
